cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BOID, please cite the associated BOID preprint. After the
  peer-reviewed journal article is published, add and use its final citation
  where appropriate.
title: "BOID — Bernadotte Oscillator Intrinsic Dimension"
abstract: >-
  Bernadotte Oscillator Intrinsic Dimension (BOID) is a general method for
  estimating resolved oscillatory dimensionality in multichannel time series.
  It combines block-Hankel embedding and multichannel singular spectrum
  analysis with Marchenko–Pastur / Bai–Yin signal-subspace rank estimation and
  TLS-ESPRIT pole recovery. BOID is defined operationally as the number of
  retained positive-frequency oscillatory modes within a specified analysis
  band.
